course: dictionary
lesson: 6876
title: Learning the word overload
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Overload is a word with more than one meaning. It can mean putting too much weight on something, or too much of anything at all. It is built from over and load. A load is what you carry, so to overload something is to give it more than it can carry.
explain: Read the words around it to find the meaning. «A good serve is a chain from the legs through the hips and body to the arm; too many hard serves day after day can overload the shoulder.» The words too many hard serves and day after day tell you the shoulder is getting more strain than it can cope with, so overload means put too much strain on it.
explain: The same word works for machines and people. A plug with too many machines on it is overloaded. A child with too much homework may feel overloaded. Ask yourself: is something being given more than it can handle? If yes, overload fits.
fact: Overload means to put too much weight or too many things on or in something.
fact: To overload a socket means to use too many machines on one plug, which can make it overheat and may cause a fire.
fact: An overload is too much of something, more than can be handled, as in «information overload».
fact: To overload a person is to give them too much work.
fact: Overload can be a verb (to overload) or a noun (an overload).
exercise: «A good serve is a chain from the legs through the hips and body to the arm; too many hard serves day after day can overload the shoulder.» What does overload mean here? | Warm it up slowly | Give it a gentle rest | *Put too much strain on it | Make it shine brightly
exercise: Mia plugs a kettle, a heater and a hair dryer into one socket. Which word describes the socket? | *Overloaded | Tidy | Empty | Sparkling
exercise: «Information overload» means | A type of cooking | A very quiet, empty room | Reading a book with a big picture on each page | *Too much information to handle at once
test: Dad says, «Don't overload the bike with shopping.» What should you avoid? | Painting the bike red | Riding the bike to the shops | Oiling the chain | *Putting too many heavy bags on the bike
test: «Sensory overload» means feeling | *Overwhelmed by too many sights, sounds and smells at once | Happy and relaxed in a quiet room | Very sleepy after lunch | Cold and hungry
exam: Jayden's coach says, «Too many hard serves can overload the shoulder.» Which answer is true? | Overload means a cool breeze | Overload means a shoulder that is fully healed | Overload means a light, gentle load | *Overload means too much strain or weight
